<p class="mb-3">
<h3>Getting started with Copilot code review<% if !@copilot_code_review_ga %> (public preview)<% end %></h3>
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
Copilot code review gives you fast, actionable AI feedback on your code so you can start iterating towards "ready to merge" while you wait for a human reviewer. There are three ways to get a review from Copilot:
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
<ul>
  <li><%= link_to "Tag Copilot as a pull request reviewer on GitHub.com", Copilot::CODE_REVIEW_REQUEST_DOCS_URL %> from the "Reviewers" menu</li>
  <li><%= link_to "Enable automatic reviews for new pull requests on GitHub.com", Copilot::CODE_REVIEW_AUTOMATIC_DOCS_URL %> using rulesets (admin permissions required)</li>
  <li><%= link_to "Use the \"Review Changes\" button in Visual Studio Code", Copilot::CODE_REVIEW_VS_CODE_DOCS_URL %>, available when drafting a commit in the "Source Control" tab</li>
</ul>
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
Note that Copilot code review only supports a limited number of programming languages, and isn't guaranteed to spot all code problems, so you should still make sure you get a human review. For more information on Copilot code review, head to the <%= link_to "docs", Copilot::CODE_REVIEW_DOCS_URL %>.
</p>
<% if !@copilot_code_review_ga %>
<p class="mb-3">
<h3>Taking Copilot's suggestions forward with Copilot Workspace on GitHub.com</h3>
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
Alongside Copilot code review, you also have access to Copilot Workspace in the context of your pull requests, a new experience on GitHub.com where you can validate and tweak Copilot's suggestions before applying them to your branch.
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
To jump into Workspace, just click the "Open in Workspace" on a suggestion from Copilot code review on GitHub.com, or use the "Edit" button on any file. For more information on Copilot Workspace, head to the <%= link_to "docs", Copilot::WORKSPACE_FOR_PRS_DOCS_URL %>.
</p>
<% end %>
<p class="mb-3">
<h3>Getting supporting and sharing your feedback</h3>
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
We'd love to hear your feedback so we can make Copilot code review and Copilot Workspace even better.
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
When you receive a comment from Copilot, you can give feedback directly with the 👍 and 👎 buttons. You can also share your thoughts and get support in our discussions on the GitHub Community:
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
<%= link_to "Copilot code review feedback and support", Copilot::CODE_REVIEW_DISCUSSION_URL %>
<% if !@copilot_code_review_ga %>
<br>
<%= link_to "Copilot Workspace for Pull Requests feedback and support", Copilot::COPILOT_WORKSPACE_DISCUSSION %>
<% end %>
</p>

<% content_for :footer_text do %>
You are receiving this email because you or an organization administrator signed up for the Copilot code review public preview.
<% end %>
